Six build fixes, none a source change to MORK or PathMap: CMake wrapper
toolchain so zlib-ng finds the NDK; 16-byte libgcc.a shim (`INPUT(-lunwind)`);
`-C target-feature=+aes,+neon` for gxhash; drop the jemalloc feature (it fails
at *link* time on Android, `_rjem_*` undefined); and an LD_PRELOAD shim calling
`mallopt(-204, 0)` because Android heap pointer tagging collides with PathMap's
`slim_ptrs` — clean build, then Aborted on the first free(). That last one is a
blocker nobody in the workspace had, because nobody had run on silicon.

Two of my own "high" MORK blockers are now measured wrong: `/dev/shm` is never
touched by `mork run` (only the ACT paths `mork test` exercises — which also
matches your S14 finding that it is absent from `server`), and the jemalloc
worry was the wrong failure mode.

